From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:12:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp): optional icon for MCP registry services

Every service in the managed MCP picker shows the same plug icon, which
makes a list of more than a handful hard to scan, and the registry
schema has no icon field and rejects unknown keys.

A registry entry may now set `icon`:

- McpService.icon takes a `data:image/svg+xml;base64,` or
  `data:image/png;base64,` URI of at most 16,384 characters. Embedded
  images only: a remote URL is rejected, so the web app never loads an
  address from the registry file. The payload must be strict base64 that
  decodes to an SVG document or a PNG, so an empty or non-image payload
  fails registry validation instead of rendering blank.
- GET /v1/mcp-registry/services returns `icon`, null when unset.
- The picker draws an SVG as a CSS mask in the muted text colour, so it
  follows light and dark themes, a PNG as an image, and the plug
  otherwise.

A server without this field rejects a registry file that sets it, so the
server is upgraded before the file gains `icon`; the registry README says
so.

Carried on custom for registries with many services, and not proposed
from here: upstream has its own issue for the same field,
https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/issues/13294, and a draft pull
request, https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/13295, which takes a
wider set of values (https URLs, same-origin paths, and SVG, PNG or WebP
data URIs, base64 or URL-encoded, up to 32 KB). Every value accepted here
is one that pull request accepts, so a registry file written for this
patch stays valid there: drop this copy if it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
